Near the end of the aerobic zone, a pump recycles a portion of the nitrified contents back
to the beginning of the nitrification zone. This internal recirculation (IR) distinguishes MLE from
the LE process and is typical pumped at twice the flowrate of the influent but can vary anywhere
from 50–500%(Ergas & Aponte-Morales, 2014; Rossinskyi, 2018). Under anoxic conditions,
denitrifying microorganisms convert the recycled nitrate into diatomic nitrogen that off-gasses
into the atmosphere through a series of reduction reactions (Rxns. 2.5-2.8) and the overall


