are typically needed(Ergas & Aponte-Morales, 2014; Rittmann & McCarty, 2001). The recently
converted nitrogen off-gasses into the atmosphere, while the reactor contents flow through the
aerobic zone again and eventually to a clarifier where the treated effluent exits the system. A
portion of the settled sludge is returned to the influent as returned activated sludge (RAS), and
the remaining is removed as wasted activated sludge (WAS).
